problems.problem:
Let $a, b, c, d$ be positive real numbers. Prove that $d$ is an integer if and only if there are positive real numbers $e, f$ satisfying
$$\left\lfloor \frac{\left\lfloor \frac{x+a}{b} \right\rfloor + c}{d} \right\rfloor = \left\lfloor \frac{x+e}{f} \right\rfloor$$
for all real numbers $x$. (For a real $y$, $\lfloor y \rfloor$ is the greatest integer less than or equal to $y$.)
